Stage 1: RIS Phase Optimization and Validation

To find the best phase configuration for the RIS elements and verify that the closed form align_phases() method gives the optimal result. 

Testing:
1. Test different optimization methods
Exhaustive Search: Tests all possible phase combinations to find the best one. It works for small RIS sizes but becomes very slow as the number of elements increases.
Coordinate Ascent: Optimizes one RIS element at a time to improve the overall signal.
Closed Form Alignment (`align_phases()`): Calculates the optimal phase for each RIS element directly using a mathematical formula.

2. Compare the results
Compare the SNR obtained from all three methods.
Use smaller phase grids for larger RIS sizes to reduce computation time.
Check whether the closed form method achieves the highest SNR.

3. Analyze SNR and data rate
Compare optimal phase alignment with random phases for different numbers of RIS elements (N).
Plot SNR and data rate against N.
Observe how increasing RIS elements improves signal strength and communication performance.

